    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "082efe90_f0649f25",
        "filename": "service/java/com/android/server/wifi/LastMileLogger.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-20T01:49:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e When we have a connection failure, we move the trace over to mLastMileLogForLastFailure - which i think also clears the trace buffer.\n\nYep.\n\n\u003e if we could get a dump call while we are still tracing - the current trace will be logged, but then cleared and then wont we have some odd half-connection attempt logs in the trace buffer?\n\nYour understanding is correct. On a call to dump(), we output the failure that we stashed away, as well as the current contents of the kernel\u0027s trace buffer. The kernel\u0027s trace buffer will contain either a) the latest successful connection attempt following the failure, or b) an in-progress connection attempt.\n\nI think both of these can be useful. In case a), we get a success case to compare against the failure case. That could help us understand the nature of the failure. In case b), we get a way to capture traces in situations where out connection-end-reporting fails. (We capture a trace of the connection that was in-progress at the time that the user triggered the bug report.)\n\n\u003e On the success side - say we have three successes in a row, then do we keep appending to the buffer?  it seems like the buffer should be cleared when we enable tracing.\n\nThe kernel will append events to the trace buffer, until the buffer fills. When that happens, the oldest events will be discarded.\n\nThis does mean that we have to take some care, when looking at traces, to be sure that we\u0027re not looking at old and irrelevant data. But, on the up side, we\u0027re less sensitive to the connection start/end reporting logic being exactly right.\n\nDoes sound reasonable? If yes, should I elaborate on this in the docstring?",
      "parentUuid": "082efe90_beedd8d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "90dc747bf743783e279bb171131149b60935d504",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
